# Business Rules

**This is the single source of truth for product behavior.** Code implements these rules; it does not define them. If code and this document disagree, one of them is a bug. Resolve with the product owner, then fix and update both.

> **Template notice:** the entities and rules below are an illustrative example (a subscription/ordering SaaS). Replace them with the real domain. Keep the format.

- **Owner:** Product (name)
- **Last reviewed:** YYYY-MM-DD

## How to use this document

- Each rule has a stable ID (`BR-<AREA>-<NN>`). IDs are never reused; retired rules are marked **Deprecated**, not deleted.
- Reference rule IDs in code comments, test names, and PR descriptions (e.g. `def test_br_ord_04_rejects_refund_after_30_days()`).
- Every rule must be testable and unambiguous. Use MUST / MUST NOT / SHOULD in the RFC 2119 sense.
- Changes to rules go through product approval and are noted in the changelog at the bottom.

## Glossary

| Term | Definition |
|---|---|
| Tenant | A customer organization; owns all of its data |
| User | A person who belongs to one or more tenants with a role |
| Plan | A subscription tier defining limits and price |
| Order | A purchase request containing line items |
| Minor units | Smallest currency unit (cents) used for all money |

## Roles and permissions

| Action | Owner | Admin | Member | Viewer |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| View orders | Y | Y | Y | Y |
| Create orders | Y | Y | Y | N |
| Cancel orders | Y | Y | Own only | N |
| Issue refunds | Y | Y | N | N |
| Manage users | Y | Y | N | N |
| Manage billing/plan | Y | N | N | N |
| Delete tenant | Y | N | N | N |

- **BR-AUTH-01:** A tenant MUST always have at least one Owner. The last Owner cannot be removed or demoted.
- **BR-AUTH-02:** Users MUST only ever see data belonging to tenants they are members of.

## Accounts and tenants

- **BR-ACC-01:** Tenant slug MUST be unique, 3-40 chars, lowercase letters/digits/hyphens.
- **BR-ACC-02:** A user email MUST be unique across the platform (case-insensitive).
- **BR-ACC-03:** Deleting a tenant is a soft delete with a 30-day recovery window, after which data is permanently purged.
- **BR-ACC-04:** Invitations expire after 7 days and are single use.

## Plans and limits

| Plan | Seats | Orders / month | API rate (req/min) |
|---|---|---|---|
| Free | 3 | 50 | 60 |
| Pro | 25 | 5,000 | 600 |
| Enterprise | Custom | Custom | Custom |

- **BR-PLAN-01:** Exceeding the seat limit MUST block new invitations, not remove existing users.
- **BR-PLAN-02:** Exceeding the monthly order limit on Free MUST block new orders with `PLAN_LIMIT_EXCEEDED`; Pro MAY exceed and be billed overage.
- **BR-PLAN-03:** Downgrades take effect at the end of the billing period. Downgrade MUST be blocked if current usage exceeds the target plan's seat limit.

## Orders

State machine:

```
draft -> submitted -> paid -> fulfilled -> (closed)
   \         \          \
    \         \          -> refunded
     -> cancelled <------
```

| From | To | Allowed when |
|---|---|---|
| draft | submitted | At least one line item |
| submitted | paid | Payment confirmed by provider |
| submitted | cancelled | Anyone with cancel permission |
| paid | fulfilled | All items delivered |
| paid | refunded | Within refund window (BR-ORD-04) |
| paid | cancelled | NOT allowed; use refund |

- **BR-ORD-01:** An order MUST have 1-100 line items; quantity per item MUST be an integer 1-999.
- **BR-ORD-02:** Order total = sum(unit price x quantity) - discounts + tax, computed server-side in minor units. Client-supplied totals MUST be ignored.
- **BR-ORD-03:** Invalid state transitions MUST be rejected with 409 `INVALID_STATE_TRANSITION`.
- **BR-ORD-04:** Refunds are allowed within 30 days of payment. Partial refunds MUST NOT exceed the paid amount minus prior refunds.
- **BR-ORD-05:** Prices are snapshotted on the order at submission; later catalog price changes MUST NOT affect existing orders.
- **BR-ORD-06:** Order creation MUST be idempotent per `Idempotency-Key` (24 h).

## Money, tax, and currency

- **BR-MON-01:** All amounts are integers in minor units with an ISO 4217 currency code. Floating point MUST NOT be used.
- **BR-MON-02:** An order has exactly one currency; mixing currencies is rejected.
- **BR-MON-03:** Rounding: tax is computed per line, rounded half-up to the minor unit.

## Notifications

- **BR-NOT-01:** Transactional emails (receipt, invitation, password reset) MUST be sent regardless of marketing preference.
- **BR-NOT-02:** Marketing emails require explicit opt-in and MUST include unsubscribe; unsubscribes apply within 24 h.

## Data retention and privacy

- **BR-DATA-01:** Audit logs retained 1 year minimum; financial records 7 years.
- **BR-DATA-02:** A verified user deletion request MUST anonymize personal data within 30 days, retaining financial records without PII where legally required.
- **BR-DATA-03:** Users can export their personal data on request.

